# The Dockerfile COPYs whole directories (assets/opt/, assets/vscode-ext-patchs/,
# assets/etc-firewall/*/), and a directory COPY takes everything present on disk —
# tracked or not. Without this file, local build debris ships inside a public
# image: __pycache__/ from running the patchers, .DS_Store from a macOS mount,
# node_modules from a skill's dependencies, and 400 KB of run logs.
#
# Keep this list to genuine debris. Everything the build actually needs is under
# assets/ and bin/, and excluding a COPY source here fails the build rather than
# degrading it silently — which is the safe direction.

.git/
.github/

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Local evidence from the suites, never part of an image.
test/results/

# A skill may carry its own deps; they are installed at build time, not copied.
**/node_modules/

*.bundle
*.tgz
*.log
